Back in June, we tried to load UltraPenguin on an Ultra 30, but
got this message:
        ok boot /pci@1f,4000/pci@4/SUNW,hme@0,1
        Boot device: /pci@1f,4000/pci@4/SUNW,hme@0,1      File and args:
        27a800 TILO

        Couldn't get translation property
        Program terminated

We were told that we needed to get a new tftpboot.img built around
kernel 2.1.107 or later and that one would be available "soon", as
soon as the fbcon problems were resolved.

Well, its been a couple of months and it looks like we'll have physical
access to the Ultra 30 again pretty shortly and are ready to have
another go at trying to load UltraPenguin unto this machine.

So, is there a new tftpboot.img available anywhere?

